      "evidence": "template/scripts/task_content_identity.py:240-244 runs `merge-tree --write-tree` and treats any return code other than 0 or 1 as `IntegrationProofError`. design.md Risks covers the post-push stop, but nothing records or checks the Git version requirement.",
      "id": "merge-tree-git-version-unchecked",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The proof depends on `git merge-tree --write-tree`, which needs Git 2.38 or newer. On an older Git the failure surfaces as `IntegrationProofError`, which stops the repair job after the repaired head was already pushed."
