    {
      "evidence": "tests/test_autonomous_integration_contour.py:293 and :311 patch `contour.main_only_reason`. The only unmocked contour test, `test_main_only_reason_needs_a_trusted_gated_head`, covers the missing-record path, which returns before the proof runs.",
      "id": "main-only-proof-not-tested-against-real-flow",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The contour tests mock `main_only_reason`. No test runs `advance_after_repair` or `main_only_reason` end to end with a real repository, generated declaration and trusted candidate head. A wrong `generated_files(root, \"HEAD\")` source or wrong `base` wiring would not be caught."
